---
variables:
  - name: stage
    required: true
  - name: error
    required: true
  - name: attempt
    required: true
  - name: max_attempts
    required: true
  - name: context
    required: false
role: decision.error-triage
response_format: text
temperature: 0.0
---
Pipeline stage: {{ stage }}
Adaptation attempt: {{ attempt }} of {{ max_attempts }}
{% if context %}
Failure record: {{ context }}
{% endif %}
A generation unit in this pipeline step failed with:

{{ error }}

The deterministic policy declined to split it (no size pressure was measured).
Answer with exactly one action:

- retry: the failure looks transient (a timeout, a dropped connection, an
  overloaded or rate-limited server). The same request is likely to succeed.
- skip: the request itself is the problem (contradictory instructions,
  output that keeps failing validation). Retrying wastes time; the pipeline
  continues with the remaining work.
- abort: the failure makes the whole run pointless (authentication,
  billing, an unusable model, a missing source).

When you answer retry, also say whether the unit should be retried at half
size (shrink: true) or unchanged (shrink: false). Prefer shrink: true when
the record shows many concepts or fetch rounds for one unit — halving it is
cheap and may fit what the whole unit did not.
